course: dictionary
lesson: 15411
title: Springtime
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Springtime is the season between winter and summer. When you meet it in a text, look at the words around it for clues. «In springtime the buds open and the first blossom appears.» Buds opening and blossom appearing show that plants are growing again, so springtime is the time of year when new life begins.
explain: Spring does not fall in the same months everywhere. In the UK, Ireland, the USA and Canada it is roughly March to May. In Australia and New Zealand it is roughly September to November, because the seasons are the other way round in the southern half of the world. So «Springtime starts in September» could be true for a child in Sydney.
explain: Writers often use springtime to mean hope and new beginnings. «After the long, grey winter, springtime brought new hope to the village.» Swap in your meaning: a new start after a hard time fits the sentence, so the word is carrying a feeling as well as a season.
fact: Springtime is the season of spring, between winter and summer.
fact: In springtime plants start to grow, flowers bloom and many baby animals are born.
fact: Springtime brings longer days and warmer weather.
fact: In the northern half of the world, spring is roughly March to May; in the southern half, roughly September to November.
fact: Buds, blossom, frogspawn and lambs are all signs of springtime.
exercise: «In springtime the days grow longer and the weather gets warmer.» What is springtime? | The time of night when the stars shine | *The season between winter and summer | The coldest season of the year | The season straight after summer
exercise: Which months are springtime in the UK? | December to February | June to August | *March to May | September to November
exercise: «The lambs were born in springtime, and the buds opened on the trees.» Find and copy one word that shows plants starting to grow. | *buds | night | winter | lambs
test: «Springtime is when the flowers bloom and the baby animals are born.» What happens in springtime? | *Plants start to grow and flowers bloom | Leaves fall from the trees | Snow covers the ground for weeks | The days get shorter and darker
test: Ella lives in Sydney. In which months is springtime there? | March to May | June to August | December to February | *September to November
exam: Which sentence uses springtime to mean a new beginning? | «The lambs were born in the field.» | *«After the long, grey winter, springtime brought new hope to the village.» | «Springtime is the season between winter and summer.» | «The children went skating on the frozen pond.»
